        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-26T21:13:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Where does the naming originate, and what is the purpose of this function ?\nIt is not very clear from the context",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11c5fa76_044ecb11",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-26T21:24:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it means the GATT server is getting a client request. it is used to initialize the tracker in GD layer.",
      "parentUuid": "0116668e_f86ce8f9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "252373e3_be81f93d",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-03T22:00:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what I am reading, it is called when the CCC descriptor is written for the CP characteristic. Don\u0027t you mean to invoke this callback from OnWriteCharacteristic instead ?\n\nIn any case I think the naming should be changed to more accurately reflect the context.",
      "parentUuid": "11c5fa76_044ecb11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34fbdacd_89c04b81",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-04T18:03:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OnWriteCharacteristic is too generic and can be called many times, I just wanted to find an entry point to initialize the cs tracker in GD. and only the kRasControlPointCharacteristic is subscribed each time. another option is to \u0027trigger it on GATT connected\u0027 but the GATT connected doesn\u0027t mean the measurement is going to happen. If you prefer it is a literally name, how about \u0027OnRasControlPointSubscribed\u0027?",
      "parentUuid": "252373e3_be81f93d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1b462fb_cd2a396d",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T17:25:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e OnRasControlPointSubscribed\n\nThat\u0027s a better naming 👍\n\n\u003e and only the kRasControlPointCharacteristic is subscribed each time\n\nSubscription is sticky if I remember correctly, i.e. after a reconnection the remote device might not necessarily write the descriptor again. Would that be an issue ?",
      "parentUuid": "34fbdacd_89c04b81",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ec253ea_4422f25f",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1583276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T17:56:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027reconnection\u0027, you didn\u0027t mean the the ACL, right? for each time an ACL is connected, this is supposed to be triggered once only; that\u0027s expected.",
      "parentUuid": "f1b462fb_cd2a396d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "232f1b71_ccd6496e",
        "filename": "system/bta/include/bta_ras_api.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1884477
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T18:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I meant ACL reaconnection yes.\nWhat I mean is that the remote device might not write the CCC descriptor on a reconnection, if it is cached by the android bt stack.\n\nFrom the GATT specification:\n\n```\n3.3.3.3. Client Characteristic Configuration\nThe Client Characteristic Configuration declaration is an optional characteristic descriptor that defines how the characteristic may be configured by a specific client. The Client Characteristic Configuration descriptor value shall be persistent across connections for bonded devices.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "2ec253ea_4422f25f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "c6b39608c7a419c6df652f1c22c9fcb9f8f466f4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
